Subject: Vulkan: Fix robust-init when OOB-self-image-copying

The front-end has logic to initialize the destination texture when the
target of glCopyTexImage2D is out of bounds of the source framebuffer.
This is not done when the destination is the same as the source however,
as that would clear the source before the copy.  This robust-init is
done by the backend in the specific case that's not done by the
front-end.

Bug: chromium:550302121
Change-Id: I4ed3de79dde184b9881746c5d8d87a6c1ef18176
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8342030
Commit-Queue: Amirali Abdolrashidi <abdolrashidi@google.com>
Auto-Submit: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Amirali Abdolrashidi <abdolrashidi@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
ANGLE on this branch predates "Remove Own* types and rename Source* types
to Owner*" (272d37f4cc): copyImage() receives a gl::OwnImageIndex and
TextureState exposes toSourceIndex() instead of toOwnerIndex(). The new
robust-init clear therefore reads the image description via
mState.getImageDesc(ownIndex.getUntranslated()) and passes
mState.toSourceIndex(ownIndex).get() (the translated gl::ImageIndex) to
stageRobustResourceClearWithFormat(), matching the surrounding code in
this file. New gl_tests/expectations entries are dropped (test-only
conflicts); the Vulkan backend change is unchanged.

diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/TextureVk.cpp b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/TextureVk.cpp
index ee06b61c321d110c77afb174be924f074613b277..073808819fa31b946e2c513f0d7f1ae73310c20b 100644
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/TextureVk.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/TextureVk.cpp
@@ -1410,6 +1410,23 @@ angle::Result TextureVk::copyImage(const gl::Context *context,
 
     if (isSelfCopy)
     {
+        // The front-end is unable to stage a robust init clear during self-copies because that
+        // would clear the source (which is the same as destination) before the copy.  That has to
+        // be done by the front-end.
+        if ((context->isWebGL() || contextVk->isRobustResourceInitEnabled()) &&
+            sourceArea != clippedSourceArea)
+        {
+            const gl::ImageDesc &desc = mState.getImageDesc(ownIndex.getUntranslated());
+            const vk::Format &format =
+                contextVk->getRenderer()->getFormat(desc.format.info->sizedInternalFormat);
+
+            ASSERT(mImage);
+            ANGLE_TRY(mImage->stageRobustResourceClearWithFormat(
+                contextVk, mState.toSourceIndex(ownIndex).get(), desc.size,
+                format.getIntendedFormat(),
+                format.getActualImageFormat(getRequiredFormatSupport())));
+        }
+
         if (!hasCopyArea)
         {
             return angle::Result::Continue;
